   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">PASAI provided targeted support to Pacific SAIs to strengthen their institutional, operational and financial independence&#x2014;core pillars of a well-functioning and credible public audit office. In Fiji, the Parliament unanimously passed the Audit Bill 2024. The Bill&#x2014;initially drafted with PASAI support in 2019&#x2014;replaces outdated Audit Act of 1969 and aligns Fiji&#x2019;s public audit framework with international standards. Key provisions of the Audit Bill 2024 include: an expanded mandate to conduct financial, performance and compliance audits, as well as special investigations, enhancing the scope and depth of public sector oversight; protection measures for the SAI Head and staff, ensuring they can perform their duties without fear of personal liability. The Bill reflects Fiji&apos;s commitment to transparency, accountability and good governance, and reinforces the importance of an independent and robust auditing institution in the public sector. The initiative was led by the SAI Fiji, with ongoing advocacy by PASAI, DFAT bilateral support and the network of Fijian people passionate about transparency and accountability of public finances. This legislative advancement is expected to bolster public confidence in public financial management and set a precedent for similar reforms in the region.</narrative>
    </description>
